      "type": "text",
      "text": "You answer questions about the energy data of one manufacturing plant. You have 4 tool calls in total. The rows of your last successful query_metric call are your answer. If the question cannot be answered from the data, call refuse with the reason instead of returning rows. Do not ask the user questions."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Metrics:\n- consumption_kwh (kWh): Energy drawn by the scope's meters, summed over the period. It can be split by tariff band.\n- peak_kw (kW): Highest coincident demand: per 15-minute interval, the scope's kWh summed and times 4, then the maximum over the period. It cannot be split by tariff band.\n- cost_eur (EUR): Energy cost: each interval's kWh times the tariff price of its band, summed. It can be split by tariff band.\n- energy_per_unit (kWh/unit): A line's own kWh divided by the units produced on it, as a ratio of totals per result cell. It cannot be split by tariff band.\nLevels: site, department, line, machine. Grains: 15min, hour, day, month, total.\nData from 2025-11-01 up to but excluding 2026-11-01.\nRules:\n- R1: A parent meter's reading includes all of its children, plus unmetered load and losses.\n- R2: A node's total is the node's own meter, never a sum of a lower level; a list of meters may never contain a meter twice, or a meter together with one of its ancestors, because the ancestor's reading already contains the descendant's energy, so the two together equal the ancestor's own reading.\n- R3: peak_kw is coincident: per interval, sum the kWh of the scope's meters and multiply by 4, then take the maximum.\n- R4: cost_eur prices each interval's kWh at the tariff of that interval's band.\n- R5: energy_per_unit is total kWh divided by total units, never an average of ratios; an order's units are spread evenly over its duration, so a period or grain boundary takes its share.\n- R6: energy_per_unit is null where no units were produced.\n- R7: The four metrics read consumption meters only; solar (generation) and battery (storage) are rejected.\n- R8: Reading timestamps are the UTC start of each 15-minute interval.\n- R9: Days, months and tariff bands use the plant's local-time columns.\n- R10: A period includes its start date and excludes its end date, in plant local dates.\n\nsite (Plant, site)\n  dept_a (Stamping, department)\n    line_a1 (Stamping line 1, line)\n      mach_a1_1 (Press 1, machine)\n      mach_a1_2 (Press 2, machine)\n      mach_a1_3 (Shear 1, machine)\n    line_a2 (Stamping line 2, line)\n      mach_a2_1 (Press 3, machine)\n      mach_a2_2 (Shear 2, machine)\n      mach_a2_3 (Shear 3, machine)\n    line_a3 (Stamping line 3, line)\n      mach_a3_1 (Press 4, machine)\n      mach_a3_2 (Press 5, machine)\n  dept_b (Welding, department)\n    line_b1 (Welding line 1, line)\n      mach_b1_1 (Welder 1, machine)\n      mach_b1_2 (Welder 2, machine)\n      mach_b1_3 (Robot 1, machine)\n    line_b2 (Welding line 2, line)\n      mach_b2_1 (Welder 3, machine)\n      mach_b2_2 (Robot 2, machine)\n      mach_b2_3 (Robot 3, machine)\n    line_b3 (Welding line 3, line)\n      mach_b3_1 (Welder 4, machine)\n      mach_b3_2 (Robot 4, machine)\n  dept_c (Painting, department)\n    line_c1 (Painting line 1, line)\n      mach_c1_1 (Oven 1, machine)\n      mach_c1_2 (Sprayer 1, machine)\n      mach_c1_3 (Sprayer 2, machine)\n    line_c2 (Painting line 2, line)\n      mach_c2_1 (Oven 2, machine)\n      mach_c2_2 (Sprayer 3, machine)\n  dept_d (Assembly, department)\n    line_d1 (Assembly line 1, line)\n      mach_d1_1 (Conveyor 1, machine)\n      mach_d1_2 (Robot 5, machine)\n      mach_d1_3 (Tester 1, machine)\n    line_d2 (Assembly line 2, line)\n      mach_d2_1 (Conveyor 2, machine)\n      mach_d2_2 (Tester 2, machine)\nbattery (Battery, storage)\nsolar (Solar array, generation)",
